{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 140,
    "dDurationMs": 4389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It makes intuitive sense that objects like\ncircles and spheres are round - but what is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4529,
    "dDurationMs": 1861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it about a sphere that makes it round?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6390,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you're talking about how effective a shape\nis at enclosing a large volume, you mean \"sphericity\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12030,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And a sphere is the shape that contains the\nmost volume with the least surface area, that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15650,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is, a sphere is the most \"spherical\" shape."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18390,
    "dDurationMs": 3139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But roundness has more to do with rolling\nthan with volume, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21529,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A round object can roll smoothly - like a\nwheel or ball bearing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25189,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the main feature that ball bearings need\nin order to roll smoothly is to be the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27949,
    "dDurationMs": 1970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "width from bottom to top/one side to the other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29919,
    "dDurationMs": 4311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It turns out there are plenty of non-circular\n'shapes of constant width' that are excellent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34230,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bearings as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35370,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Reuleaux rotor, for example, is made up\nof segments from three circles intersecting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39480,
    "dDurationMs": 4690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at their centers - so every point on a side\nis the same distance from the opposite corner,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44170,
    "dDurationMs": 1639,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the rotor rolls around wonderfully."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45809,
    "dDurationMs": 5091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, the Reuleaux rotor can even turn\nsmoothly in a square hole!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50900,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But don't try to use a Reuleaux rotor for\nthe wheel on your car - since they're not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53200,
    "dDurationMs": 2030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a constant distance from the axle, those points\nwill make for a bumpy ride!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55230,
    "dDurationMs": 3899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, the points on a Reuleaux rotor are\njust that - pointy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59129,
    "dDurationMs": 3051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Doesn't that go against the idea of roundness?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62180,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Geology has the answer: stones with sharp\nor rough edges that are worn away become \"rounded.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67720,
    "dDurationMs": 4090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we might say a Reuleaux rotor is round\nbut not rounded."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71810,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand, certain British coins are\nround AND rounded, though they're still not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75920,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "circles: the 20 and 50-p coins are shapes\nof constant width, which means they look un-circularly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82000,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cool but don't get stuck in coin machines!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84220,
    "dDurationMs": 5090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And isn't if funny that \"rouleau\" means \"roll\"\nin French and Franz Reuleaux invented a rolling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89310,
    "dDurationMs": 15140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rotor?"
    } ]
  } ]
}
